Z||000017||stimpy||06-21-2001||01:28 PM||||Sounds like you could get it for a grand. I'd snap it up in a heartbeat if I were you, unless it has suspension problems. I paid $2500 for my 86 GT with the same miles and comparable condition. Screw the wing though. I'd use that coupla hundred bucks to open up an enngine rebuild bank account. It will need one eventually, but at that price it's still a great deal. You could bring it to Oklahoma and double your money right away...||||reg||1
Z||000018||Ken Wittlief||06-21-2001||01:43 PM||||if it failed its smog test then check out the tail pipes for soot, and see if it smells rich when its running.<P>  just because it failed its smog test, and it has an exhaust leak, doesnt mean the 2nd caused the first - it could be the cause, or it could be one of several other problems that can make it run rich (stuck injectors, rings are shot, burning oil, bad sensor on the ECM system...||||reg||1
Z||000019||Ken Wittlief||06-21-2001||01:45 PM||||and dont forget to run the VIN # through carfax if you can.||||reg||1
Z||000020||DisfourDan||06-21-2001||01:51 PM||||well the VIN is 1G2PG3793FP234914 ,  I went to carfax and they found 3 files on it.  But they say I have to order it to see what they are.  Anyone know of a place that does it for free?  ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Ken Wittlief||06-21-2001||02:11 PM||||the 3 files doesnt mean they found three things wrong with it (but they do word it to make you think you better pay the $15 and find out)<P>  it could be three times the car was titled, or smog tests - prob the last one is the failed smog test.<P>  maybe someone here still has a account - mine expired.||||reg||1
Z||000022||DisfourDan||06-21-2001||02:21 PM||||My brother called me and told me the car was in very good condition, he is going to test drive it in a day or so.  I was reading on the Fiero Recalls, and was wondering, is the problem with this car, the problem they fix in the recall?||||reg||1
Z||000023||DRH||06-21-2001||05:20 PM||||Start a new thread with a title like "Can someone please run a CarFax for me." and put the VIN number in it. I believe some members have accounts but may not see it down in this thread. <P>Looks like a good deal unless something else is wrong. Offer about 900 and take it for 1000 to 1100. Front manifold is probably cracked. Not the easiest thing in the world to fix, but well worth the difference in what it would be worth. It's actually not too bad to fix as long as no bolts break off...<P>||||reg||3
Z||000024||Kelvin Vivian||06-21-2001||06:38 PM||||The front logo appears to be missing and so is the the rear "Fiero GT" lettering on the decklid. My guess is that these were probably removed for a repainting.<P>At $1,200, price is excellent. Just make sure to have your brother check it out good.<BR>I like it. Looks smooth wingless, but you want a wing, you can always can pick one up on eBay.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402874&Sequence=1&res=high">  <BR>88 GT, 5-spd<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||14
